{"metadata":{"symbolKind":"module","roleHeading":"Framework","title":"AmplitudeEncoding","modules":[{"name":"AmplitudeEncoding"}],"externalID":"AmplitudeEncoding","role":"collection"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records to an Amplitude project through its HTTP V2 API."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/amplitude(apiKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)"},{"type":"text","text":" makes an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations"},{"type":"text","text":") for your Amplitude project in one call. It checks"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the API key, posts to the HTTP V2 endpoint of the project’s data residency ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeRegion"},{"type":"text","text":")"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with an "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":", and splits each batch to Amplitude’s limits"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder\/batchLimit"},{"type":"text","text":"): 10 events and 1 MB a request, which a project on any plan"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accepts. A batch with no record the encoder can write, an empty one included, makes no request. It"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"retries no response, a 5xx, 408 and 429, and drops and reports any other status. The API key goes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in the body, so no header field is needed, and no trace context is sent. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"leaves this module out; import it on its own."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The region has no default. A project’s data resides in Amplitude’s default data center or its EU"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one, and an event posted to the other doesn’t reach it, so you pick the region on purpose. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"factory throws "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeSetupError","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for an empty key, and for an Amplitude Experiment deployment"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"key, which isn’t the project’s API key."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each record becomes an event of an anonymous device. Its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"device_id"},{"type":"text","text":" is the record’s session,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from the sessions enricher, and its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"session_id"},{"type":"text","text":" that session’s start in Unix milliseconds; a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record with no session is sent under its own record identifier, with no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"session_id"},{"type":"text","text":". No "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"user_id"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is sent. Its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"insert_id"},{"type":"text","text":" is the record’s identifier, which a redelivered record keeps, and its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"time"},{"type":"text","text":" the record’s timestamp in epoch milliseconds. The record’s vendor identifier and trace"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"context aren’t sent, nor is an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ip"},{"type":"text","text":", and the standard context is sent as Amplitude’s own fields"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"app_version"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"device_model"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"language"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"platform"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"os_name"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"os_version"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Amplitude counts a user per ","type":"text"},{"code":"device_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and bills by monthly tracked users, so each session counts","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as one tracked user, and so does each record sent without a session.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan"},{"text":" the encoder is made with, into","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"event_properties"},{"text":". A ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals. A record the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"encoder can’t write is left out and the rest of the batch is sent: one the plan doesn’t describe,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one whose event name Amplitude keeps for its own (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[Amplitude] …"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$identify"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$groupidentify"},{"text":"),","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one whose event isn’t ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"text":", one holding a value JSON can’t, one whose timestamp has no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"epoch-milliseconds form, and one too large for a request. The destination reports each as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)"},{"text":", a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"text":" whose reason is an ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeEncodingError"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To send to PostHog, use ","type":"text"},{"code":"PostHogEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instead.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import AmplitudeEncoding","import HTTPDestinations","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let amplitude = try HTTPDestination.amplitude(","    apiKey: apiKey,","    region: .us,  \/\/ or .eu, where the project's data resides","    plan: plan)","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: amplitude)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers what Amplitude receives, and why, in more detail.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Sending to Amplitude","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/amplitude(apiKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination